ains how to create an LPBAM application, scenario, and queue with the STM32CubeMX tool.\nThe LPBAM functionality of the STM32CubeMX tool is based on the LPBAM software utility in STM32U5 Cube Firmware. It is an easy-to-use feature that was introduced as a standalone menu.","playlistId":"PL8n_tqwYdzVDE2e7v8m0oTV6F9SYQFeqL","position":29,"publishedAt":"2022-09-28T08:49:53Z","resourceId":{"kind":"youtube#video","videoId":"d8Fc8pK843o","videoUrlCN":"https://www.stmcu.com.cn/video/2464","encodedThumbnail":"","encodedThumbnailmq":""},"thumbnails":{"default":{"height":90,"url":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/d8Fc8pK843o/default.jpg","width":120},"high":{"height":360,"url":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/d8Fc8pK843o/hqdefault.jpg","width":480},"maxres":{"height":720,"url":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/d8Fc8pK843o/maxresdefault.jpg","width":1280},"medium":{"height":180,"url":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/d8Fc8pK843o/mqdefault.jpg","width":320},"standard":{"height":480,"url":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/d8Fc8pK843o/sddefault.jpg","width":640}},"title":"STM32CubeMX - Design low-power background autonomous mode application","videoOwnerChannelId":"UCjnmZw3h4XnpK3e5D2jvIGA","videoOwnerChannelTitle":"STMicroelectronics","duration":"PT5M51S"}},{"etag":"BzFQ7AIqWVA8YoEIY3-ASnao6lw","id":"UEw4bl90cXdZZHpWREUyZTd2OG0wb1RWNkY5U1lRRmVxTC5DRUQwODMxQzUyRTlGRkY3","kind":"youtube#playlistItem","snippet":{"channelId":"UCp2oBOA52LnGp3C5PqlfBeg","channelTitle":"STM32CubeMX","description":"Find out more information: https://bit.ly/LPBAM-STM32U5\n\nThe Low Power Background Autonomous Mode (LPBAM) is a powerful new feature of the STM32U5 microcontroller that allows peripherals to run autonomously with optimized power consumption down to STOP 2 mode. In this video, you will learn about how the LPBAM works and go through the creation of an example project that utilizes the LPBAM.\n\nHere are some useful links if you would like to learn more about the LPBAM:\n\nAN5645: STM32U5 Series power optimization using LPBAM\nhttps://bit.ly/AN5645\n\nRM0456: STM32U575 Reference Manual\nhttps://bit.ly/RM-0465\n\nSTM32U575 Datasheet:\nhttps://bit.ly/STM32U575-Datasheet\n\n\nBelow is the necessary code for the example project in the video:\n\n/* Modify STM32U575ITXQ_FLASH.ld */\n\nMEMORY\n{\n  RAM(xrw): ORIGIN = 0x28000000,LENGTH = 16K\n  FLASH(rx): ORIGIN = 0x08000000,LENGTH = 2048K\n}\n\n\n/* main.c USER CODE BEGIN Includes */\n\n#include \"lpbam_txapp.h\"\n\n\n\n/* main.c USER CODE BEGIN PV */\n\nuint8_t SPIBuff[] = {0x12};\nuint8_t UARTBuff[] = {'!'};\nDMA_HandleTypeDef *LPDMA_Handlers[2] =\n{\n    &handle_LPDMA1_Channel0,\n    &handle_LPDMA1_Channel1\n};\n\n\n\n\n/* lpbam_txapp_txdata_build.c USER CODE BEGIN EV */\n\nextern uint8_t SPIBuff[];\nextern uint8_t UARTBuff[];\n\n\n\n/* main.c USER CODE BEGIN 2 */\n\nMX_TXApp_Init();\nMX_TXApp_TxData_Init();\nMX_TXApp_TxData_Build();\nMX_TXApp_TxData_Link(LPDMA_Handlers[0]);\nMX_TXApp_TxData_Start(LPDMA_Handlers[0]);\n\n__HAL_RCC_PWR_CLK_ENABLE();\nHAL_PWREx_EnterSTOP2Mode(PWR_STOPENTRY_WFI);\n\n\n\n/* lpbam_txapp_txdata_config.c USER CODE BEGIN TXApp_TxData_Start \n * in MX_TXApp_TxData_Start() \n */\n\nif (HAL_LPTIM_PWM_Start(&hlptim1, LPTIM_CHANNEL_1) != HAL_OK)\n{\n  Error_Handler();\n}\nif (HAL_LPTIM_PWM_Start(&hlptim3, LPTIM_CHANNEL_1) != HAL_OK)\n{\n  Error_Handler();\n}","playlistId":"PL8n_tqwYdzVDE2e7v8m0oTV6F9SYQFeqL","position":30,"publishedAt":"2023-11-07T13:55:26Z","resourceId":{"kind":"youtube#video","videoId":"NQep_EYf1po","videoUrlCN":"https://www.stmcu.com.cn/video/2853","encodedThumbnail":"","encodedThumbnailmq":""},"thumbnails":{"default":{"height":90,"url":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/NQep_EYf1po/default.jpg","width":120},"high":{"height":360,"url":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/NQep_EYf1po/hqdefault.jpg","width":480},"maxres":{"height":720,"url":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/NQep_EYf1po/maxresdefault.jpg","width":1280},"medium":{"height":180,"url":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/NQep_EYf1po/mqdefault.jpg","width":320},"standard":{"height":480,"url":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/NQep_EYf1po/sddefault.jpg","width":640}},"title":"Configuring LPBAM applications on the STM32U5 with STM32CubeMX","videoOwnerChannelId":"UCjnmZw3h4XnpK3e5D2jvIGA","videoOwnerChannelTitle":"STMicroelectronics","duration":"PT13M26S"}},{"etag":"9oJjfoMMYxSNBW7FQkyKzQ9nbas","id":"UEw4bl90cXdZZHpWREUyZTd2OG0wb1RWNkY5U1lRRmVxTC45NkVENTkxRDdCQUFBMDY4","kind":"youtube#playlistItem","snippet":{"channelId":"UCp2oBOA52LnGp3C5PqlfBeg","channelTitle":"STM32CubeMX","description":"In order to replicate the tutorial instructions in your environment, please ensure you have loaded STM32CubeMX with the X-CUBE-AZRTOS-WL.pack\n•   Use the shortcut Alt-U or click on the following menu on STM32CubeMX toolbar:\n  Help - Manage embedded software packages\n•   Then select\n  STMicroelectronics panel - enable X-CUBE-AZRTOS-WL\n\nIn addition to that, depending on your STM32CubeMX Project Manager settings, you may need to copy manually the ThreadX middleware in the \\Middleware\\ST\\ directory of your firmware package for the compilation to be successful.\n\n•   RF projects in the STM32CubeWL MCU package :  www.st.com/stm32cubewl\n\n•   STM32CubeMX : www.st.com/microxplorer\n\n•   X-CUBE-AZRTOS-WL : www.st.com/x-cube-azrtos-wl\n\nFind out more info : www.st.com/stm32cube","playlistId":"PL8n_tqwYdzVDE2e7v8m0oTV6F9SYQFeqL","position":31,"publishedAt":"2022-06-10T09:57:31Z","resourceId":{"kind":"youtube#video","videoId":"Me0WnR2DOQk","videoUrlCN":"null","encodedThumbnail":""},"thumbnails":{"default":{"height":90,"url":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Me0WnR2DOQk/default.jpg","width":120},"high":{"height":360,"url":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Me0WnR2DOQk/hqdefault.jpg","width":480},"maxres":{"height":720,"url":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Me0WnR2DOQk/maxresdefault.jpg","width":1280},"medium":{"height":180,"url":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Me0WnR2DOQk/mqdefault.jpg","width":320},"standard":{"height":480,"url":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Me0WnR2DOQk/sddefault.jpg","width":640}},"title":"STM32WL - How to port an exis